WEBVTT

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.360
Our first match's duelists are now arriving!

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.980
They're Crow Hogan and Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:14.830
Gongenzaka?

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:15.820
Gongenzaka?

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.930
Gonny?

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.900
Why not me?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.500
I'm the one who should shine 
in the opening spotlight! Me!

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.820
The man Gongenzaka will show 
you the power of the Lancers.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.760
I don't want to be a show for them. 
But if I must, I'll win.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:53.730
I'm going to win and show the 
kids what we can really do!

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.580
It's rotten luck that we have to 
work on a day like this...

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.200
No kidding.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.140
Go on in.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.020
That went perfectly.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:07.770
Yeah.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.120
Hey! Try to walk straighter!

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.280
What's with that guy?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.590
Wait a minute!

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.520
Ow...

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:19.960
Hey, you three!

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:20.750
Run!

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.500
Hurry!

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:22.990
Wait for me!

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.560
D-Wheels.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:29.770
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:29.770 --> 00:01:31.470
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:34.920
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.050
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.340
Opening Battle!! 
Crow Versus Gongenzaka

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:20.560
City's biggest duel event, the Friendship 
Cup, is about to begin!

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.320
Will the first winner be Crow or Gongenzaka?

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.360
Mr. Atlas is a Tops hero.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.100
Could you not lump him in with them?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.420
King, my butt! He's a traitor!

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.060
Jack is a Commons hero!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.030
Hey, are you guys listening to me?

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.830
What's going on at this tournament?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.460
I'm gonna start, okay? Action Field, on.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.320
Field Spell Crossover Acceleration!

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:57.450
Duel mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.290
Frank! Amanda! Tanner!

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.510
What are they...

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.090
Riding duel...

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.960
Acceleration!

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:14.090
Duel!

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.570
Crow Hogan is slow out of the gate!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.220
Did they come here to cheer me on?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.180
What were they thinking?!

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:30.900
Will Gongenzaka be the first 
to round the corner?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.230
He's going to crash!

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:43.260
In that case, I need to end this fast.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:47.230
Crow Hogan is the first around the 
corner, securing the first turn!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.310
Cheering for Jack makes you a traitor, too!

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.200
What was that?

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.670
I'm trying to make this exciting, you know...

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:57.980
Wait!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.580
My turn!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.110
When there are no cards on the field,

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:05.660
I can Special Summon Blackwing — 
Gust the Backblast from my hand.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.620
When a Blackwing is on the field,

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.060
I can also Special Summon Tuner Monster Blackwing 
— Oroshi the Squall from my hand.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:25.240
Level 1 Oroshi the Squall tunes 
Level 2 Gust the Backblast!

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.580
Ebony wings, pierce the heavens and soar.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.040
Synchro Summon!

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.180
Come out, Assault Blackwing — 
Kuniyoshi the White Rainbow!

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.310
Completing a Synchro Summon in the first turn...

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:43.220
You are a worthy opponent.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.310
What?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.530
What is he looking for?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.960
Once per turn, Kuniyoshi the White Rainbow

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:01.570
lets me send one Blackwing to the graveyard, 
to deal you 300 points of damage!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:06.780
On his first turn, Crow Hogan uses 
a monster effect to deal damage!

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.480
No, I need to focus on the duel.

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:14.450
And I summon Tuner Monster Blackwing 
— Blizzard the Far North!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.060
When I successfully summon this card,

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:25.100
I can Special Summon one Blackwing, 
Level 4 or below, from the graveyard.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:30.800
I Special Summon Blackwing — Jetstream the 
Blue Sky, which I sent to the graveyard!

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:40.620
Level 2 Blizzard the Far North tunes 
Level 1 Jetstream the Blue Sky!

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.990
Ebony wings, tear through the heavens in a flash!

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.190
Synchro Summon!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.810
Come out, Assault Blackwing — 
Kunisada the White Rainbow!

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:56.070
Two Synchro Monsters?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.400
But their attack points are both just 1000.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.130
No match for me yet.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:03.000
Once per turn, Kunisada the White Rainbow

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:06.840
can return one Blackwing, Level 3 or below, 
from my graveyard to my hand,

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.220
increasing the attack points of Synchro 
Summoned Blackwings

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.380
by that monster's attack points 
until the end of my turn!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:18.550
Their attack points increase by Blizzard's 1300!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.390
2300 attack points?

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:25.020
On the turn I use this effect, I cannot battle.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.540
I end my turn.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.350
What's wrong, Crow? Why are you in such a hurry?

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:36.600
But my immovable spirit will not be shaken.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.570
It doesn't matter what I'm riding.

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:41.230
Where are they? Where?

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.540
They weren't caught, were they?

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.780
He's looking into the stands again.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.580
Hey, you! What are you looking at?

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:52.490
We're in the middle of a duel! Face me!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:55.620
That's the basic courtesy you owe your opponent!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.820
My turn! Draw!

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:04.040
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Magnet from my hand!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:07.400
When I successfully summon this card,

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:12.830
I can Special Summon one Superheavy Samurai 
monster, Level 4 or below, from my hand.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:15.590
Come out, my second Magnet!

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:21.400
When Superheavy Samurai Magnet is on the field,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.120
it's the only monster you can attack.

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:27.820
In other words, with two Superheavy Samurai 
Magnets on my side of the field,

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.960
they both protect my other monsters, 
and you can't attack either of them.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:35.630
This is one form of the immovable 
duel that I have chosen.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.100
I end my turn!

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.990
He's trying to slow me down.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.170
My turn! Draw!

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:55.150
Kunisada the White Rainbow's effect ends, 
and their attack points return to normal.

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.080
I activate Kuniyoshi the White 
Rainbow's monster effect!

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.890
I send Blackwing — Harmattan 
the Dust to the graveyard,

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.900
to deal 300 damage to you!

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.590
He did it again.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:10.560
Crow Hogan is slowly chipping away 
at his opponent's life points.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.300
And I summon Blizzard the Far North!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.270
Blizzard the Far North's monster effect

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:21.240
lets me Special Summon Harmattan 
the Dust from my graveyard!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:29.660
Kuniyoshi's effect lets him send a Blackwing 
to the graveyard, dealing effect damage,

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:34.480
and then he can use Blizzard's effect 
to Special Summon that monster.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.190
An extremely efficient summoning method.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.360
Now, let's finish this quickly.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:44.060
Harmattan the Dust can add the level of 
one Blackwing on the field to its own.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.630
I choose Level 3 Kuniyoshi the White Rainbow.

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.630
Spread your ebony wings,

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.770
and strike the ground with the speed of lightning!

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.240
Synchro Summon!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.980
Rain down, Assault Blackwing — 
Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.230
Three Synchro Monsters?

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:06.030
Once per turn, Raikiri the Rain Shower 
can destroy cards on your field

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.220
equal to the number of Blackwings on my field.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:10.920
My Superheavy Samurai Magnets 
can't be destroyed by battle,

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:12.460
so you'll destroy them with effects?

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.120
There are three Blackwings 
on my side of the field.

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.700
I destroy your two Superheavy Samurai Magnets!

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:23.370
Gongenzaka's immovable defense has crumbled!

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:26.730
I attack directly with Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.420
Raikiri the Rain Shower's attack points are 2600.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.580
If that attack goes through, his life 
points will plunge to 800!

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:37.980
An Action Card!

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.950
Action Cards are spell cards, 
spread out over the duel field.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:45.900
Can Gongenzaka use it to avoid the damage?!

00:10:56.730 --> 00:11:00.120
I attack directly with Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:03.910
An Action Card!

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:07.880
Can Gongenzaka use it to avoid the damage?!

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:10.010
He ignored it!

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:10.980
What?

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:13.650
Gongenzaka!

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.160
Gongenzaka didn't use the Action Card.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.870
He just took the 2600 damage!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:28.800
Isn't your group's style to use Action Cards?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.150
This is his style.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.000
What's going on?

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.710
You did a brilliant job of crushing 
my immovable defense.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.690
But when I take damage from a direct attack,

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.240
without spell or trap cards in my graveyard,

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.980
I can Special Summon this card 
in defense position.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:49.640
Come out, Superheavy Samurai Prepped Defense!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.090
Is that why he didn't use the Action Card?

00:11:54.090 --> 00:11:56.680
But it has 2100 defense points.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:59.190
I'll end it next turn!

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:02.330
Wait for me, Frank, Amanda, Tanner!

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:04.370
I end my turn.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.340
My turn! Draw!

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:13.480
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1 
Superheavy Samurai General Jade

00:12:13.480 --> 00:12:15.850
and Scale 8 Superheavy Samurai General Coral!

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:22.420
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 7 simultaneously.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.180
Pendulum Summon!

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:30.090
Come out, Tuner Monster Superheavy 
Samurai Trumpeter!

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.320
Superheavy Samurai Flutist!

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.550
They were Special Summoned at the same time?

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:39.770
So he can use Pendulum Summon, too?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.290
Once per turn, Superheavy Samurai General Jade

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:51.370
can increase the level of one Superheavy 
Samurai on my side of the field!

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.950
I increase Superheavy Samurai 
Trumpeter's level to 3!

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.090
Level 3 Superheavy Samurai Trumpeter

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:03.020
tunes Level 3 Superheavy Samurai Prepped Defense 
and Level 3 Superheavy Samurai Flutist!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:08.860
As immovable as mountains, the soul 
that dwells in great rocks...

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.600
Come to dwell in the land, as a fortress!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.070
Synchro Summon!

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:17.940
Appear, Level 9 Superheavy 
Samurai Beast Kyubi!

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:22.600
From Pendulum to Synchro Summon?

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:23.770
That little...

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.050
He evolved without even notifying me.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.020
And he got the crowd really riled up!

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.040
Great one, Gongenzaka!

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.990
He's pretty good!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.740
No way... The crowd's going wild?

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:38.460
Now, will Gongenzaka begin his counterattack?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:43.790
For every Special Summoned monster 
on your side of the field,

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:45.950
Superheavy Samurai Beast Kyubi's 
defense points increase by 900.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.910
You have three. Thus, they increase by 2700!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.880
5200 defense points?

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:56.490
In addition, this monster can attack from faceup 
defense position, using its defense points!

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.250
Attacking from defense position?

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.630
When it does, it can only attack 
the monster on your field

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.820
with the highest attack points!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.890
I attack Raikiri the Rain Shower!

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.940
Crow Hogan takes 2600 damage all at once!

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.730
I think it's over.

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:25.930
When a Superheavy monster 
destroys a monster by battle,

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.080
Superheavy Samurai General 
Jade's Pendulum Effect

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:33.420
allows it destroy itself, so Superheavy Samurai 
Beast Kyubi can attack once more.

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.550
Once more? Oh, no.

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:37.420
If only it were in defense position...

00:14:37.420 --> 00:14:40.350
Right now, Kyubi's defense points are 4300.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:43.440
If it attacks the 1000-attack-point 
Kunisada the White Rainbow,

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.640
you'll take 3300 points of damage. 
This will be over!

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:50.900
Are you so sure?

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.270
Until the end, you don't know 
how a battle will go.

00:14:53.270 --> 00:14:55.000
No, I know.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:59.690
Duels are a match with your opponent, 
but also a battle with yourself.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.940
A man with a wavering heart cannot defeat me!

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.020
They're...

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.610
Frank...

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:11.690
Run!

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:13.640
Let's go!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.990
Wait!

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.000
Are they the cause of your distraction?

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.870
Who are those children?

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:49.030
At first, I just planned to feed them 
and then kick them right out.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:55.090
Slow down... You'll choke.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.320
Are you okay?

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.270
Tanner!

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:02.970
You've got a mustache!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.610
So do you, Amanda.

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:07.420
You, too, Frank!

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:08.280
Me, too?

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.560
You've got a mustache!

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:12.880
Don't laugh! You have one, too!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.570
A mustache!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.220
You kids...

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.520
I hadn't smiled like that in years.

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:23.150
In the end, I let them stay.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:28.710
If not for them, I don't know what 
would have happened to me.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:33.270
That's why I want to be a role model for them.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.520
The reason I agreed to take part 
in this tournament was

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:41.580
to win and to prove that we 
could do something, too.

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.920
A role model?

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.120
Which means, if I beat you...

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:54.520
Go, Crow!

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:58.460
We'll be fine! So, Crow, do your best!

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:02.430
Crow Hogan!

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:05.150
You want to be a role model to those children?

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:08.880
Then duel me with everything you've got!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:15.220
Shouldn't you be showing those 
children a real duel right now?

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:22.190
Now, come at me, Crow. 
Let us show no mercy.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:27.840
I destroy Superheavy Samurai General Jade 
to let Kyubi attack a second time!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.700
Go, Superheavy Samurai Beast Kyubi!

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:35.300
Attack Kunisada the White Rainbow!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.270
Is this the end?

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.310
I activate Action Card Evasion!

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:44.740
I negate one monster attack!

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:50.680
Crow Hogan used an Action 
Card to skirt certain doom!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.590
You have magnificent riding technique.

00:17:57.590 --> 00:18:02.020
But the monster on your side of the field 
only has 1000 attack points!

00:18:02.020 --> 00:18:04.500
You cannot defeat Superheavy 
Samurai Beast Kyubi.

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:06.560
I end my turn!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.960
During the End Phase of my turn,

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:13.870
if Superheavy Samurai Jade is the only monster 
in my Pendulum Zones, it is destroyed!

00:18:15.020 --> 00:18:17.140
4300 defense points...

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:20.480
My turn! Draw!

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:23.680
I activate my spell card Against the Wind!

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:29.400
I add Blizzard the Far North to my hand, 
and take its attack points as damage!

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.540
Intentionally taking all that damage?

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.190
I like your spirit.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.040
Come at me, Crow!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.400
I summon Blizzard the Far North!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:45.600
I activate Blizzard the Far North's monster effect!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.840
Come out, Jetstream the Blue Sky!

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:55.670
Level 2 Blizzard the Far North tunes 
Level 1 Jetstream the Blue Sky!

00:18:58.210 --> 00:19:02.050
Ebony sword, echo with these wings!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.520
Synchro Summon!

00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:07.980
Come out, Assault Blackwing — 
Kunifusa the White Rainbow!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:10.860
Another Synchro Monster on the field

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:13.960
increases Superheavy Samurai 
Beast Kyubi's defense points!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:17.150
When Assault Blackwing — 
Kunifusa the White Rainbow

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:22.710
is Synchro Summoned with a Blackwing as 
a component, it can be used as a Tuner!

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:24.940
What? A Tuner?

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:28.650
Level 3 Kunifusa the White Rainbow 
tunes Level 3 Kuniyoshi

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.110
and Kunisada the White Rainbow.

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:38.040
Ebony wings, spread amidst 
the gathering clouds,

00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.630
and become the sword that bisects the heavens!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.830
Synchro Summon!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:48.630
Descend, Assault Blackwing — 
Kusanagi the Gathering Storm!

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:55.310
A Synchro Summon using 
three Synchro Monsters?

00:19:57.270 --> 00:20:00.940
Crow Hogan has completed his Synchro Summon!

00:20:00.940 --> 00:20:04.920
With fewer Synchro Monsters now on the 
field, Kyubi's defense points decrease.

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:06.090
Great, Crow!

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:07.150
Go!

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:09.080
Let's go, Gongenzaka.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:13.680
Until the End Phase of the turn when Kusanagi 
was successfully Synchro Summoned,

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:19.060
its attack points increase by those of the 
Blackwings used to Special Summon it.

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:21.030
6000 attack points?

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:26.270
Battle! I attack Superheavy Samurai Beast Kyubi 
with Kusanagi the Gathering Storm!

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:30.740
But Kyubi is in defense position. Even if 
you defeat it, I won't take damage!

00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:36.270
When Kusanagi the Gathering Storm attacks a monster 
in defense position, it deals piercing damage!

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:37.180
What?

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.260
Gonny!

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:53.520
He did it!

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:57.640
Crow Hogan wins the opening match 
with a dramatic victory!

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:02.300
All right!

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:03.570
Crow won!

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:08.480
Attacking from defense position?

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:10.540
Your monsters really do cheat.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.060
Crow!

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.420
Great job, Crow!

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:20.330
Uh-oh.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:21.870
Let's go, Amanda... Tanner.

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:23.100
Wait!

00:21:23.100 --> 00:21:25.360
Crow, good luck next round, too!

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:26.900
We'll be back to cheer you on!

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:29.870
Let us through!

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:37.780
Congratulations.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:41.240
You showed me your real duel.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:44.810
Gongenzaka...

00:21:50.750 --> 00:21:52.430
That was really moving, Crow!

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:53.960
A magnificent duel!

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.880
The spectators, who were arguing before...

00:23:45.680 --> 00:23:48.410
Hey! How have you been, Yuya?

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:49.920
Mr. Tokumatsu?

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:52.540
I thought you couldn't leave your room...

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:54.950
Don't sweat the details!

00:23:55.540 --> 00:23:58.120
The truth is that I heard an odd rumor.

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:00.590
They say that those who lose in the Friendship Cup

00:24:00.590 --> 00:24:03.520
are conscripted into forced labor beneath City.

00:24:03.520 --> 00:24:05.220
Forced labor?

00:24:06.220 --> 00:24:10.060
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
City's Light and Shadow.

00:24:10.060 --> 00:24:12.130
The fun is only getting started!
